{%- comment -%}
  Lockup per docs/10-logo.md, drawn in HTML/CSS rather than SVG.

  The spec is proportional, so em units express it natively — and the mark cannot
  break when the brand name changes length, which matters given docs/18-name-clearance.md.
  (The previous SVG had a fixed 420-unit viewBox sized for "Hikari" and clipped
  anything longer.)

  Against a Latin font-size of 1em, cap height C ≈ 0.70em, so:
    kanji   1.30 C  → 1.035em       (one weight step below the Latin)
    rule    1.00 C  → 0.70em tall
    clear   0.55 C  → 0.42em either side
    Latin   tracked 0.28em

  scale: "hero" → kanji 200 / Newsreader 300 / rule 1px
  scale: "body" → kanji 300 / Newsreader 400 / rule 1.3px   (small sizes, print, signage)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign s = scale | default: 'body' -%}
{%- if s == 'hero' -%}{%- assign kw = 200 -%}{%- assign lw = 300 -%}{%- assign rw = '1px' -%}
{%- else -%}{%- assign kw = 300 -%}{%- assign lw = 400 -%}{%- assign rw = '1.3px' -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign name = settings.brand_name | default: shop.name -%}
<span class="lockup" style="font-size:{{ size | default: '20px' }}" role="img" aria-label="{{ name | escape }}">
  <span class="lk-k" style="font-weight:{{ kw }}" aria-hidden="true">{{ settings.brand_kanji | default: '光' }}</span>
  <span class="lk-r" style="border-left-width:{{ rw }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="lk-n" style="font-weight:{{ lw }}" aria-hidden="true">{{ name }}</span>
</span>
